wDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","number":25,"title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":341,"closed_issues":2335,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T03:07:42Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":8,"created_at":"2026-01-28T18:27:30Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T10:08:54Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.6.stable\n- Not reproducible in 4.5.1.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon(TM) RX Vega 11 Graphics (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 31.0.21910.5) - AMD Ryzen 5 2400GE with Radeon Vega Graphics (8 threads) - 15.68 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen running a scene for the first time after startup while having a Window Width/Height Override set in the Project settings, the sizing is incorrect. For example, if running a project with Window Width/Height Override of 1280x720 the first time running the scene will result in the window size being 1228x691. Running the scene a second time will result in the window size correctly being 1280x720. A print readout on a _ready function shows that the window size should be 1280x720, but using a _process function to check each frame shows that it is resized to 1228x691 after the _ready function.\n\n<img width=\"1919\" height=\"1037\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/daa5f363-f24c-4d9b-b5d1-35d1dc9a489c\" />\n\n<img width=\"1195\" height=\"726\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ea121a8a-92d1-467f-9b79-de58cc974370\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a new project and save a scene of any node type. Go into project settings, enable advanced settings and set the Window Width/Weight Override setting under the Window tab to anything other than the Viewport Width/Height. Run the current scene and check the size displayed in the top right corner of the embedded game window. Alternatively, attach a script to the scene with the following functions:\n```\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tprint(get_window().get_size())\n\nfunc _process(_delta: float) -> void:\n\tprint(get_window().get_size())\n```\n\nThe printout should show the first ready print as the initial override values, then they are replaced by the new unwanted values on the first process frame onwards.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nThis may fall under N/A as it requires very minimal setup to recreate from a brand new project, but I have added simple project just in case.\n\n[window_bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24918776/window_bug.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115523/reactions","total_count":9,"+1":6,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":3},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115523/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}